WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.722
Step three is routing, but only when more than one source is possible.

00:00:04.722 --> 00:00:12.477
For teaching, a simple rule can check whether the word order appears and then route to both policy and order data.

00:00:12.477 --> 00:00:15.317
That makes the idea easy to see.

00:00:15.317 --> 00:00:19.325
But do not confuse a teaching rule with a production router.

00:00:19.873 --> 00:00:28.740
A real project might extract order I D's deterministically, then use structured model output only for ambiguous intent.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:35.510
For example, if the user says, where is my package, the route may be order tracking.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:40.955
If the user says, what are your shipping rules, the route may be policy retrieval.

00:00:41.548 --> 00:00:44.180
Start with the simplest reliable rule.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:49.471
Add semantic routing only when keyword or deterministic logic is not enough.
